<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ADMIRAL POSTS 18-MONTH LOSS, NO DIV.</title>
<headline>ADMIRAL POSTS 18-MONTH LOSS, NO DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>18 months ended August 31 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		 </p>
<p>    - attrib		  5.43 loss</p>
<p>    - headline		4.11 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     1.88   </p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss	    0.64   </p>
<p>    Tax			 0.78    </p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.06   </p>
<p>    Turnover		  16.92    </p>
<p>Full name: Admiral Leisure World Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of assoc	  0.45 loss</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.46 gain    </p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said no comparative figures were presented</p>
<p>as the group was formed on March 1, 1995.</p>
<p>They said the group would apply for the full spectrum of</p>
<p>gaming licences, will manage gaming operations and supply</p>
<p>equipment. It is planned to buy interests in international</p>
<p>gaming operations to reduce the risk of rand-denominated</p>
<p>investments, they said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
